Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant tables & columns and why they matter  
• legislators.gender ­– filter for “F” (female) legislators.  
• legislators.id_bioguide – join key to legislators_terms.  
• legislators_terms.id_bioguide – connects a legislator to her terms.  
• legislators_terms.term_number – 0 = first term → tells us the state she first represented.  
• legislators_terms.state – state abbreviation we finally want to count.  
• legislators_terms.term_start, legislators_terms.term_end – check whether any of a legislator’s terms included a 31‑Dec date.  
Main conditions we will need  
1. legislators.gender = 'F'  
2. A term contains 31‑Dec of at least one year in its span.  One pragmatic SQL‑lite test is:  
      date(term_start) ≤ date(substr(term_end,1,4)||'-12-31')  
  AND date(term_end)   ≥ date(substr(term_end,1,4)||'-12-31')  
   (i.e. the 31‑Dec of the end year falls inside the term)  
3. Select state from the legislator’s FIRST term (term_number = 0).  
4. Count legislators once each, group by that first‑term state, pick the largest count.

Below are ten exploratory → final SQLs (all limited to 20 rows unless a final aggregate).  
Each is preceded by a short comment describing its purpose.

```sql
-- 1. See the possible gender values that exist.
SELECT DISTINCT gender
FROM legislators
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Quick count of how many female legislators are in the table.
SELECT COUNT(*) AS female_legislators
FROM legislators
WHERE gender = 'F';
```

```sql
-- 3. Inspect the first few term records to confirm column names / formats.
SELECT *
FROM legislators_terms
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Look at the distribution of term_number values for female legislators.
SELECT DISTINCT term_number
FROM legislators_terms lt
JOIN legislators l
  ON l.id_bioguide = lt.id_bioguide
WHERE l.gender = 'F'
ORDER BY term_number
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. List female legislators’ first‑term states (term_number = 0).
SELECT l.id_bioguide,
       lt.state,
       lt.term_start,
       lt.term_end
FROM legislators_terms lt
JOIN legislators l
  ON l.id_bioguide = lt.id_bioguide
WHERE l.gender = 'F'
  AND lt.term_number = 0
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Spot‑check any female legislator terms that END on 31‑Dec.
SELECT lt.id_bioguide,
       lt.term_start,
       lt.term_end
FROM legislators_terms lt
JOIN legislators l
  ON l.id_bioguide = lt.id_bioguide
WHERE l.gender = 'F'
  AND lt.term_end LIKE '%-12-31'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. More general test: female terms that *contain* 31‑Dec of the END year.
SELECT lt.id_bioguide,
       lt.term_start,
       lt.term_end
FROM legislators_terms lt
JOIN legislators l
  ON l.id_bioguide = lt.id_bioguide
WHERE l.gender = 'F'
  AND date(lt.term_start) <= date(substr(lt.term_end,1,4) || '-12-31')
  AND date(lt.term_end)   >= date(substr(lt.term_end,1,4) || '-12-31')
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Which female legislators (id) satisfy the 31‑Dec criterion (deduplicated)?
SELECT DISTINCT lt.id_bioguide
FROM legislators_terms lt
JOIN legislators l
  ON l.id_bioguide = lt.id_bioguide
WHERE l.gender = 'F'
  AND date(lt.term_start) <= date(substr(lt.term_end,1,4) || '-12-31')
  AND date(lt.term_end)   >= date(substr(lt.term_end,1,4) || '-12-31')
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Map those qualifying legislators to the state of their FIRST term.
SELECT l.id_bioguide,
       first_term.state
FROM legislators l
JOIN legislators_terms first_term
     ON first_term.id_bioguide = l.id_bioguide
WHERE l.id_bioguide IN (
        SELECT DISTINCT lt.id_bioguide
        FROM legislators_terms lt
        JOIN legislators l2
          ON l2.id_bioguide = lt.id_bioguide
        WHERE l2.gender = 'F'
          AND date(lt.term_start) <= date(substr(lt.term_end,1,4) || '-12-31')
          AND date(lt.term_end)   >= date(substr(lt.term_end,1,4) || '-12-31')
     )
  AND first_term.term_number = 0
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Final answer: count of qualifying female legislators by their first‑term state,
--     ordered to show the state with the highest count.
SELECT first_term.state          AS state_abbrev,
       COUNT(DISTINCT l.id_bioguide) AS female_legislator_count
FROM legislators l
JOIN legislators_terms first_term
     ON first_term.id_bioguide = l.id_bioguide
WHERE l.gender = 'F'
  AND first_term.term_number = 0
  AND l.id_bioguide IN (
        /* any term that contains a December 31 */
        SELECT DISTINCT lt.id_bioguide
        FROM legislators_terms lt
        JOIN legislators l2
          ON l2.id_bioguide = lt.id_bioguide
        WHERE l2.gender = 'F'
          AND date(lt.term_start) <= date(substr(lt.term_end,1,4) || '-12-31')
          AND date(lt.term_end)   >= date(substr(lt.term_end,1,4) || '-12-31')
     )
GROUP BY first_term.state
ORDER BY female_legislator_count DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

Run the final query: the first row produced will give  
• state_abbrev – the state whose female cohort is largest under the December‑31 condition  
• female_legislator_count – how many such legislators.
